</span></td>
<td id="A3.T2.7.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.2pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:69.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T2.7.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">str_replace_editor</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T2.7.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.2pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:189.8pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T2.7.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Four subcommands under a single tool: </span><span id="A3.T2.7.2.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">view</span><span id="A3.T2.7.2.3.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;"> reads a file by line range or lists a directory to depth two; </span><span id="A3.T2.7.2.3.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">create</span><span id="A3.T2.7.2.3.1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;"> writes a new file; </span><span id="A3.T2.7.2.3.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">str_replace</span><span id="A3.T2.7.2.3.1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;"> replaces a uniquely matched string within an optional line range; and </span><span id="A3.T2.7.2.3.1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">insert</span><span id="A3.T2.7.2.3.1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;"> inserts content after a specified line. Long outputs are truncated according to the budget.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T2.7.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T2.7.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.2pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:58.7pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T2.7.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Command execution</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T2.7.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.2pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:69.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T2.7.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">bash</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T2.7.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.2pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:189.8pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T2.7.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Executes arbitrary shell commands in a persistent shell session inside the container, including navigation, directory inspection, scripted search, and background jobs. It supports soft timeouts and standard-input (STDIN) injection, and returns standard output and exit code, with hard truncation for overlong output.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T2.7.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T2.7.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.2pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:58.7pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T2.7.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Incremental compilation</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T2.7.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.2pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:69.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T2.7.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">compile_code</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T2.7.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.2pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:189.8pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T2.7.4.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Triggers an incremental build through </span><span id="A3.T2.7.4.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">build.sh</span><span id="A3.T2.7.4.3.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;"> under the current repository state, classifies failure causes into </span><span id="A3.T2.7.4.3.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">code_error</span><span id="A3.T2.7.4.3.1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">, </span><span id="A3.T2.7.4.3.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">timeout</span><span id="A3.T2.7.4.3.1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">, </span><span id="A3.T2.7.4.3.1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">out_of_memory</span><span id="A3.T2.7.4.3.1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">, </span><span id="A3.T2.7.4.3.1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">system_limit</span><span id="A3.T2.7.4.3.1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">, and </span><span id="A3.T2.7.4.3.1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">environment_error</span><span id="A3.T2.7.4.3.1.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">, and returns structured error lists and logs. This is the only executable-feedback source for the outcome-level reward component </span><math id="A3.T2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\text{compile}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">r</mi><mtext mathsize="0.700em">compile</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\text{compile}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.T2.7.4.3.1.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T2.7.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T2.7.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.2pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:58.7pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T2.7.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Task tracking</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T2.7.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.2pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:69.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T2.7.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">task_tracker</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T2.7.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.2pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:189.8pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T2.7.5.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Maintains a structured task list through </span><span id="A3.T2.7.5.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">view</span><span id="A3.T2.7.5.3.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;"> and </span><span id="A3.T2.7.5.3.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">plan</span><span id="A3.T2.7.5.3.1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">, with states </span><span id="A3.T2.7.5.3.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">todo</span><span id="A3.T2.7.5.3.1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">, </span><span id="A3.T2.7.5.3.1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">in_progress</span><span id="A3.T2.7.5.3.1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">, and </span><span id="A3.T2.7.5.3.1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">done</span><span id="A3.T2.7.5.3.1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">, allowing the policy to explicitly organize repair plans and progress over long multi-turn trajectories.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T2.7.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T2.7.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.2pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:58.7pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T2.7.6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Explicit termination</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T2.7.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.2pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:69.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T2.7.6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">finish</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T2.7.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.2pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.6.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:189.8pt;">
<span id="A3.T2.7.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T2.7.6.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">A trajectory-termination action actively emitted by the policy, indicating that the repair is complete and should be settled. After it is triggered, no subsequent actions are accepted and reward computation begins directly.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The semantic judge uses Kimi-K2.5 as the backend. Its input is {compilation error description, model-generated patch list, minimal-sufficient GT repair patch list}, where the GT repair is the minimal sufficient repair defined in Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Training Data Construction ‣ 3 Method ‣ Signal Reshaping for GRPO in Weak-Feedback Agentic Code Repair" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>. Its output includes intent consistency, confidence, and detailed analysis. Scoring is based strictly on semantic equivalence and functional consistency, without requiring identical code style or implementation, and lexical similarity is not used as the reward. The implementation keeps only two semantic outcomes, <span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">consistent</span> and <span id="A3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">inconsistent</span>: the former maps to <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=1</annotation></semantics></math> under the layered reward, while the latter, skipped semantic checks, or semantic-judge failures retain compilation-only partial credit <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> on compiled samples. Semantic checking is retried at most two times during training and at most five times during evaluation, both with exponential backoff. The reliability of this judge is audited on a <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="400" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>400</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">400</annotation></semantics></math>-sample human-annotated subset stratified by method and judge label in Appendix <a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 Semantic Judge Validation: 400-Sample Human Audit ‣ Appendix C Environment and Tool-Interface Implementation Details ‣ Signal Reshaping for GRPO in Weak-Feedback Agentic Code Repair" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Minimal sufficient repairs and recent-change clues.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The data-refinement pipeline only removes content from the original developer patch; it never adds, rewrites, or reorders patch lines. An LLM is given the compilation error, error types, and original diff, and is asked to return a strict subset together with an error-to-line mapping and removal rationale. The generated patch is first checked with <span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">git apply --check</span>/<span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">git apply</span> and then verified by running the build script in the failing build directory. If the refined patch fails to apply or compile, the pipeline retries once in a conservative mode; if it still fails, it falls back to the original developer patch. Only compile-verified outputs are marked as successful refinement and compilation. Recent-change clues are produced by extracting source files from the compiler error log, finding the previous commit for each file at the corresponding repository revision with <span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">git log</span>, and retrieving the pre-failure diff with <span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">git diff</span>; these clues are included in the sample’s initial prompt text, so training and evaluation use the same injection path.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Retention Rates of the Data-Construction Pipeline</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ C.1 Retention Rates of the Data-Construction Pipeline ‣ Appendix C Environment and Tool-Interface Implementation Details ‣ Signal Reshaping for GRPO in Weak-Feedback Agentic Code Repair" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> summarizes the per-stage retention from internal compilation-infrastructure logs to the final curated train/evaluation pool. Stage retention is computed relative to the previous stage, and cumulative retention is computed relative to the initial <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12{,}618" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>12,618</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12{,}618</annotation></semantics></math> raw compilation-error directories. The historical-diff augmentation step adds context to each sample and does not further filter the sample pool.</p>
</div>
