</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Semantic Judge Validation: 400-Sample Human Audit</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Both layered rewards and step-level process scores rely on the Kimi-K2.5 semantic judge. We treat it as a reward proxy and audit it offline; the audit does not change the training loop.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Protocol.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The audit covers four checkpoints—GRPO-compile-only, GRPO-binary, GRPO-early (post-fork tail), and GRPO-full (final)—to characterize judge reliability <em id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">across</em> methods and training stages, not only on the final main-method checkpoint. From each checkpoint’s <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="400" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>400</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">400</annotation></semantics></math>-sample evaluation split, we stratify-sample <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> judge-<span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">consistent</span> and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> judge-<span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">inconsistent</span> compile-success patches, for <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> patches per checkpoint and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="400" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>400</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">400</annotation></semantics></math> patches in total. Compile-failure cases are excluded since the judge is not invoked. Two annotators familiar with the C/C++ build system independently label each patch as consistent or inconsistent with the GT minimal sufficient repair, blind to the judge’s verdict and to the source checkpoint; a third annotator adjudicates disagreements.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Results.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Results. ‣ C.2 Semantic Judge Validation: 400-Sample Human Audit ‣ Appendix C Environment and Tool-Interface Implementation Details ‣ Signal Reshaping for GRPO in Weak-Feedback Agentic Code Repair" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> combines the pooled confusion matrix and aggregate reliability metrics. The two annotators agree on <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="372/400=0.930" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>372</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>400</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.930</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">372/400=0.930</annotation></semantics></math> cases, and the judge agrees with the adjudicated human label on <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="360/400=0.900" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>360</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>400</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.900</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">360/400=0.900</annotation></semantics></math> cases; precision/recall/<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> on the <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">consistent</span> class are <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.880/0.917/0.898" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.880</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>0.917</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>0.898</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.880/0.917/0.898</annotation></semantics></math>. The slight precision–recall gap reflects a mild over-acceptance tendency typical of reference-conditioned LLM-as-judge on code. Per-checkpoint agreement is tightly clustered in <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[89\%,91\%]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>89</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>91</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[89\%,91\%]</annotation></semantics></math> (GRPO-compile-only: <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="89/100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>89</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">89/100</annotation></semantics></math>, GRPO-binary: <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="90/100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">90/100</annotation></semantics></math>, GRPO-early: <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="90/100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">90/100</annotation></semantics></math>, GRPO-full: <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="91/100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>91</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">91/100</annotation></semantics></math>), with no clear method-specific bias.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T4.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="A3.T4.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Confusion matrix and reliability metrics for the <math id="A3.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="400" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>400</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">400</annotation></semantics></math>-sample human audit. Confidence intervals use Wilson for proportions and bootstrap (<math id="A3.T4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math>k resamples) for <math id="A3.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
