</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Disagreement categories.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Of the <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>40</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40</annotation></semantics></math> mismatches: <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FP <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=24</annotation></semantics></math></span> (judge says consistent, human says inconsistent)—symptom-level fixes that suppress the diagnostic (<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math>), unrelated behavior changes such as different fallback or extra logging (<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math>), and coarser-granularity workarounds such as disabling a warning (<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math>); <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FN <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=16</annotation></semantics></math></span> (judge says inconsistent, human says consistent)—functionally equivalent repairs at different locations or surface forms (<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math>), and alternate correct repair paths over-weighted as lexically divergent from GT (<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math>). FP outnumbers FN by a moderate margin (<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>24</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">24</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math>), consistent with the well-documented over-acceptance bias of LLM-as-judge on code; the bias is distributed similarly across the four source checkpoints (<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> test, <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.74" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.74</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.74</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Supplementary note on the post-fork comparison.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The judge is a bounded-noise reward proxy, not an oracle. The audit shows mild over-acceptance (FP <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>24</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">24</annotation></semantics></math> vs. FN <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math>), corresponding to an approximately <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.0</annotation></semantics></math>pp net offset in absolute success rate. Because GRPO-full and GRPO-early use the same judge, this offset mainly affects absolute levels; per-checkpoint judge–human agreement clusters in <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[89\%,91\%]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>89</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>91</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[89\%,91\%]</annotation></semantics></math>, with no visible leniency toward GRPO-full over GRPO-early. Thus, the audit is only a supplementary check on the post-fork <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5.0</annotation></semantics></math>pp increment, reducing the likelihood that it is entirely due to differential judge bias.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Paired significance and bias-corrected human-equivalent accuracy of the post-fork <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+5.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+5.0</annotation></semantics></math>pp.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since GRPO-full and GRPO-early are evaluated on the same <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="400" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>400</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">400</annotation></semantics></math>-sample hint-free split, we run a paired McNemar test on <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">compile_and_semantic</span>: the contingency (both correct <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="176" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>176</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">176</annotation></semantics></math>, only-full <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="36" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>36</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">36</annotation></semantics></math>, only-early <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math>, both wrong <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="172" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>172</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">172</annotation></semantics></math>) gives <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}=(36-16)^{2}/(36+16)\approx 7.69" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>36</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>36</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>7.69</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}=(36-16)^{2}/(36+16)\approx 7.69</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\approx 0.006" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.006</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\approx 0.006</annotation></semantics></math>), with a Wilson <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="95\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">95\%</annotation></semantics></math> CI of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[+0.018,+0.082]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.018</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.082</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[+0.018,+0.082]</annotation></semantics></math> for the paired difference, excluding zero. Applying Rogan–Gladen judge-bias correction with the audit-derived sensitivity <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.917" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.917</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.917</annotation></semantics></math> and specificity <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.885" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.885</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.885</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{\text{true}}=(p_{\text{obs}}-(1-\text{spec}))/(\text{sens}+\text{spec}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>true</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>obs</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mtext>spec</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>sens</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>spec</mtext></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{\text{true}}=(p_{\text{obs}}-(1-\text{spec}))/(\text{sens}+\text{spec}-1)</annotation></semantics></math>, denominator <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.802" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.802</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.802</annotation></semantics></math>), the human-equivalent rates are <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.455" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.455</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.455</annotation></semantics></math> (GRPO-early) and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.517" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.517</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.517</annotation></semantics></math> (GRPO-full)—a corrected gap of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+6.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+6.2</annotation></semantics></math>pp, slightly larger than the raw <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+5.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+5.0</annotation></semantics></math>pp; FP rates on <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">consistent</span>-judged patches for GRPO-full vs. GRPO-early (<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5/50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5/50</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6/50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6/50</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}=0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}=0.10</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.75" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.75</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.75</annotation></semantics></math>) further rule out method-specific judge leniency. The post-fork increment therefore survives both paired statistical inference and reasonable judge-bias correction.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Dataset and Repository Scale</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To characterize both the workload of the <em id="A3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">repair task</em> itself and the size of its <em id="A3.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">repair context</em>, we measure four scale metrics per sample: (i) the repository-side <span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">source file count</span>—the number of files in the repository subtree under C/C++ extensions (<span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">.c/.cc/.cpp/.cxx</span>, the corresponding header families, and <span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">.inc/.inl/.ipp</span>) plus the companion <span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">.proto</span> IDL files; (ii) the repository-side <span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">source LOC</span>—the total line count of those files; (iii) the <span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">number of GT-modified files</span>; and (iv) the <span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">number of GT-changed lines</span>—i.e., the modified-file count and the combined added/deleted line count of the minimal sufficient repair patch. Figure <a href="#A3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ C.3 Dataset and Repository Scale ‣ Appendix C Environment and Tool-Interface Implementation Details ‣ Signal Reshaping for GRPO in Weak-Feedback Agentic Code Repair" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> reports the empirical CDFs of these four metrics on the train and eval splits.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2605.07276v1/fig_dataset_scale.svg" id="A3.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/113;" width="476" height="113"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="A3.F4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Distributions of repository scale and GT-modification scale across the <math id="A3.F4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}510" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,510</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}510</annotation></semantics></math> samples (train <math id="A3.F4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}110" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,110</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}110</annotation></semantics></math> + eval <math id="A3.F4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="400" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>400</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">400</annotation></semantics></math>). Each curve is the empirical CDF of one split; the <math id="A3.F4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>-axis is logarithmic in (a)(b)(d) and linear in (c). Source-file statistics include only C/C++ files and the companion <span id="A3.F4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">.proto</span> IDL, excluding build artifacts, logs, and configuration files.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Strong asymmetry between read and write scale.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Across the <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}510" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,510</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}510</annotation></semantics></math> samples, the per-repository C++ source-file count has median <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}339" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,339</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}339</annotation></semantics></math> and maximum <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4{,}135" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4,135</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4{,}135</annotation></semantics></math>, while source LOC has median <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\sim}3.08\!\times\!10^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.608em;" width="0.608em"><mo>∼</mo></mpadded><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sim}3.08\!\times\!10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math> and maximum <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\sim}9.18\!\times\!10^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.608em;" width="0.608em"><mo>∼</mo></mpadded><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sim}9.18\!\times\!10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math> (Figure <a href="#A3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ C.3 Dataset and Repository Scale ‣ Appendix C Environment and Tool-Interface Implementation Details ‣ Signal Reshaping for GRPO in Weak-Feedback Agentic Code Repair" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>(a)(b)). In contrast, the number of GT-modified files has median <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{75}\!=\!1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>75</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{75}\!=\!1</annotation></semantics></math>, and maximum <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>; the total GT-changed line count has median only <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{75}\!=\!7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>75</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{75}\!=\!7</annotation></semantics></math>, and maximum <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="378" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>378</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">378</annotation></semantics></math> (Figure <a href="#A3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ C.3 Dataset and Repository Scale ‣ Appendix C Environment and Tool-Interface Implementation Details ‣ Signal Reshaping for GRPO in Weak-Feedback Agentic Code Repair" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>(c)(d)). The policy must therefore localize <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> files and <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(10)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(10)</annotation></semantics></math> lines of precise edits within a context of <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>-scale files and <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math>-scale LOC—the <em id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">read scale exceeds the write scale by roughly <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math> times</em>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Train/eval alignment.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The train and eval curves in Figure <a href="#A3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ C.3 Dataset and Repository Scale ‣ Appendix C Environment and Tool-Interface Implementation Details ‣ Signal Reshaping for GRPO in Weak-Feedback Agentic Code Repair" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> overlap on all four metrics: source-file count and LOC have similar medians (train: <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}393" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,393</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}393</annotation></semantics></math> files / <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.26\!\times\!10^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.26\!\times\!10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math> LOC; eval: <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}172" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,172</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}172</annotation></semantics></math> files / <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.68\!\times\!10^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.68\!\times\!10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math> LOC), and only the right tail of the train split extends slightly further toward larger repositories (max <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4{,}135" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4,135</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4{,}135</annotation></semantics></math> files / <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9.18\!\times\!10^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9.18\!\times\!10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math> LOC vs. eval’s <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3{,}300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3,300</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3{,}300</annotation></semantics></math> files / <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6.68\!\times\!10^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6.68\!\times\!10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math> LOC). The GT-modification scale is essentially identical between splits, supporting distributional comparability of fixed-split evaluation metrics.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>GRPO Training Hyperparameters and Sampling Budget</h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ C.4 GRPO Training Hyperparameters and Sampling Budget ‣ Appendix C Environment and Tool-Interface Implementation Details ‣ Signal Reshaping for GRPO in Weak-Feedback Agentic Code Repair" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> summarizes the training, rollout, and optimizer configuration shared by the main experiments and ablations. The optimizer follows AdamW <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite> with decoupled weight decay.</p>
</div>
