<section id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">C1–C5 inference results.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We inject hints during inference on <math id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="400" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>400</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">400</annotation></semantics></math> evaluation samples at the step-<math id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="239" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>239</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">239</annotation></semantics></math> checkpoint, using temperature <math id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.7</annotation></semantics></math> and pass@1. The results are shown in Table <a href="#A5.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ C1–C5 inference results. ‣ E.5 Hint-Type Construction and Selection ‣ Appendix E Core Prompt Design ‣ Signal Reshaping for GRPO in Weak-Feedback Agentic Code Repair" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. C3, an NL strategy summary of approximately <math id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="180" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>180</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">180</annotation></semantics></math> words, obtains the highest pass@1 of <math id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="53.5\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>53.5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">53.5\%</annotation></semantics></math>, improving over the no-hint baseline of <math id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="44.5\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>44.5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">44.5\%</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+9.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>9.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+9.0</annotation></semantics></math>pp. C1 provides only <math id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+2.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+2.5</annotation></semantics></math>pp because it contains too little information, while C4 and C5 cause more fallback cases because of information overload, yielding lower net gains than C3.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A5.T8.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Table 8</span>: </span><span id="A5.T8.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Inference results for five NL hint granularities at step <math id="A5.T8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="239" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>239</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">239</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A5.T8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="400" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>400</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">400</annotation></semantics></math> samples.</span></figcaption>
